# Implement LangGraph Workflow (Phase 2)

We will build the LangGraph orchestration to convert raw text into a structured audio drama script using the Groq API (Llama-3 models) and Qdrant.

## Open Questions

> [!WARNING]
> Please confirm if you have set `GROQ_API_KEY` in your `.env` file, as the agents will use Groq by default for Llama-3. I've defaulted to `llama-3.1-8b-instant` for the Director/Reviewer and `llama-3.3-70b-versatile` for the ScriptWriter.
> If you prefer to use local Ollama, please let me know, and I can switch the LLM initialization to `ChatOllama`.

## Proposed Changes

### `app/schemas/script.py`
Define the expected Pydantic output.
#### [NEW] `app/schemas/script.py`
- `ScriptLine(BaseModel)`: `speaker: str`, `text: str`, `emotion: str`
- `Script(BaseModel)`: `lines: List[ScriptLine]`

### `app/agents/state.py`
Define the state object passed between nodes.
#### [NEW] `app/agents/state.py`
- `AgentState(TypedDict)`: 
  - `chapter_text: str`
  - `director_breakdown: str`
  - `script: Optional[Script]`
  - `feedback: Optional[str]`
  - `revision_count: int`

### `app/agents/tools.py`
#### [NEW] `app/agents/tools.py`
- `Lore_RAG_Tool`: A LangChain `@tool` that takes a `character_name` as input, embeds the query using our `SentenceTransformer` model, and queries the Qdrant `lore_entities` collection. It returns the character's persona and voice tone.

### `app/agents/nodes.py`
Implement the agent nodes.
#### [NEW] `app/agents/nodes.py`
- **director_node**: Takes `chapter_text`, uses `llama-3.1-8b-instant` to identify characters and context. Updates `director_breakdown`.
- **scriptwriter_node**: Uses `llama-3.3-70b-versatile`. Takes `chapter_text` and `director_breakdown`. Has access to `Lore_RAG_Tool` via tool calling. Generates the final script using `.with_structured_output(Script)`.
- **reviewer_node**: Uses `llama-3.1-8b-instant`. Checks if the script is complete and formatted correctly. Outputs feedback or `PASS`.

### `app/agents/graph.py`
Wire the nodes into a `StateGraph`.
#### [NEW] `app/agents/graph.py`
- Create the graph.
- Add nodes: `director`, `scriptwriter`, `reviewer`.
- Set edges: `START -> director -> scriptwriter -> reviewer`.
- Conditional edge from `reviewer`: If `PASS` or `revision_count > 3`, go to `END`. Otherwise, route back to `scriptwriter` with feedback.

### `test_graph.py`
#### [NEW] `test_graph.py`
A standalone script to execute the graph with a small piece of text and print the resulting JSON script to verify everything works.

